{
  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the image modality adds predictive signal at all — the core premise of multimodal cellular profiling. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest controlled extension of the baseline: it keeps the RNA encoder and profile setting identical to config_001, so any accuracy difference is attributable to the addition of image features via a standard resnet50 encoder and simple concat fusion. This single experiment simultaneously tests (a) whether image modality carries complementary information, (b) whether concat fusion is a viable starting point, and (c) whether resnet50 is a reasonable image encoder. If config_016 substantially exceeds 48.5%, we exploit the multimodal direction in subsequent runs; if it is comparable or worse, we learn that the image modality (at least with resnet50) is not contributing, redirecting effort toward RNA encoder or profile-setting improvements. Under a tight budget, resolving the modality question first prevents wasting experiments on hyperparameter tuning of a potentially unhelpful modality."
}

